/T (The change in model ranking is also worth noting. Gradient Boosting was strongest in the original pipeline, whereas Random Forest performed better under the trial-level analysis. This does not establish that Random Forest is generally better for EOG. It simply shows that the preferred model can depend on how the data is divided.)
/E (The change in model ranking is also worth noting. Gradient Boosting was strongest in the original pipeline, whereas Random Forest performed better under the trial-level analysis. This does not establish that Random Forest is generally better for EOG. It simply shows that the preferred model can depend on how the data is divided.)
